# Viper NGCC API_PKC submission package

`API_PKC/` is the self-contained NGCC API_PKC submission boundary for MAMBA-Viper. All formal implementations, formal NGCC KAT outputs, and NGCC API checks are contained under this directory.

## Layout

- `Implementations/Reference_Implementation/AlgorithmInstance/` is the unmodified official API_PKC template.
- `Implementations/Reference_Implementation/MAMBA-Viper-{128,192,256,384,512}/` contains C99 reference API_PKC instances.
- `Implementations/Optimized_Implementation/MAMBA-Viper-{128,192,256,384,512}/` contains optimized AVX2 API_PKC instances.
- `Test_Vectors/` contains official NGCC KAT files generated by the unmodified copied `KAT_KEM.c` in the Reference instances.
- `Internal_Tests/NGCC_API/api_check.c` contains internal API conformance checks.

## Frozen byte lengths

| Instance | VIPER_LEVEL | VIPER_USE_E8_CODEC | pk | sk | ss | ct |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| MAMBA-Viper-128 | 128 | 1 | 608 | 1424 | 16 | 736 |
| MAMBA-Viper-192 | 192 | 1 | 992 | 2200 | 24 | 1088 |
| MAMBA-Viper-256 | 256 | 1 | 1312 | 2912 | 32 | 1472 |
| MAMBA-Viper-384 | 384 | 1 | 2496 | 5488 | 48 | 2656 |
| MAMBA-Viper-512 | 512 | 1 | 3200 | 7040 | 64 | 3456 |

## Build and KAT generation

From any instance directory:

```sh
make clean
make
make kat
```

`make kat` runs the unmodified official `KAT_KEM.c`, writes `output/KAT_KEM_MAMBA-Viper-XXX.txt`, and copies formal Reference/Optimized output into `API_PKC/Test_Vectors/`. The formal submission KAT files are the files under `API_PKC/Test_Vectors/`.

## Official support files

The official `KAT_KEM.c`, `drng.c/h`, and `auxfunc.c/h` files copied into each instance are byte-for-byte identical to `Implementations/Reference_Implementation/AlgorithmInstance/`.

Viper randomness is adapted through `viper_api_rng.c`, whose `randombytes` compatibility symbol calls `get_random_number(&drng_algorithm, buf, len * 8ULL)`. Hash/XOF compatibility symbols are implemented by `viper_api_hash.c` and route through official `sm3hash`, `pseudohash`, and `pseudoXOF` from `auxfunc`.

`kem_dec` uses implicit rejection: for valid-length ciphertext inputs it computes the fallback shared secret path and returns `0`, so ciphertext invalidity is not exposed through the API return value.

Legacy PQCkemKAT vectors are internal regression vectors for the original Viper implementation. They are not the official NGCC API_PKC test vectors. Official NGCC test vectors are generated by the unmodified API_PKC KAT_KEM.c and stored under API_PKC/Test_Vectors/.
